-- Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market - its bestiary and its notable NPCs.
-- 0 creatures (migration 074) and 3 notable NPCs (migration 072),
-- with their attacks in stat_attacks (migration 073).
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~376-splynn-npcs-c.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/bestiary-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every
-- creature row passes creatureFormulaGaps, every value is printable ASCII,
-- and an 8-word shingle check of the prose fields against the book's cached text finds no copied run.

INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('high-lord-tlan', 'High Lord T''Lan', NULL, 'High Lord in charge of the Splynn Dimensional Market and its police; second authority in Splynn after Lord Splynncryth', 'rifts', 'High Lord (Splugorth High Lord species, as printed)', '10th level Tattoo Master, Line Walker and Shifter (as printed)', 10, 'Aberrant', NULL, '7 feet, 6 inches (2.3 m)', '180 lbs (81 kg)', '{"IQ":22,"ME":20,"MA":17,"PS":28,"PP":18,"PE":18,"PB":3,"Spd":16}', NULL, NULL, 400, 520, 88, NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"roll":2,"pull":2}', 'Five physical or psionic attacks per melee, or two by magic. Also +1 to strike with a body block/tackle, +1 to save vs psionics, +1 to save vs magic and +6 to save vs Horror Factor. No attack damage is printed; none is derived.', NULL, 'Skills of note, no percentages printed: several scientific fields, many languages, all lore skills, and military strategy; he is one of Splynncryth''s foremost military advisors.', 'Those of every High Lord: nightvision to 1000 feet (305 m), excellent color vision, turns invisible at will, sees the invisible, bio-regenerates 1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute, and can teleport to Lord Splynncryth at 98% once per 24 hours. He never sleeps, resting in meditation for twenty minutes at most.', 'All spell magic of levels 1-15, all Stone Master powers, the power to create Magic Tattoos, and all Shifter abilities. P.P.E. 520.', 'Major psychic: Astral Projection, Empathy, Mind Block, Object Read, Sense Magic, Speed Reading, Telepathy and Total Recall. I.S.P. 88.', NULL, NULL, 'Several sets of Bio-Wizard shackles, two or three of them D-Shackles, and a Call Staff (a greatest rune weapon). Usually wears no armor; when he expects a fight it is generally magical, and he can obtain nearly anything else he needs, rune weapons included.', NULL, 'Cool and controlled even in the middle of a surprise raid, and quick to plan an answer to it. Proud of his rank, he still puts the job first and is wholly loyal to Splynncryth; if Splynn were besieged he would stay to the end while his master teleported away. A shrewd foe who seldom misjudges an enemy, and trusted completely by his lord.', 'Lord Splynncryth; Powerlord Cronus and the D-Squads under him.', 'Dimensional Raiders.', 'A typical High Lord to look at, with very sharp teeth, long thin limbs and large eyes darker than most of his kind. For more than two centuries he has run the Market''s police and settled its trade disputes with almost no trouble, answerable to Splynncryth alone; only a Rune Master could rise above him. His Shifter magic lets him sense raiders crossing into the Market and send troops after them across the Megaverse. He can commit up to a million troops to a disturbance, and may take command of the millions of Minions in Splynn if the need is real, though he must justify it to Splynncryth.', 'Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market p.54-55'),
('powerlord-cronus', 'Powerlord Cronus', 'K''Ronn Sol', 'Head of Splynn Security; commander of the D-Squad Division', 'rifts', 'Kydian (Overlord made a Powerlord by Bio-Wizard augmentation)', '12th level Powerlord, Head of Splynn Security (as printed)', 12, 'Aberrant', '32 years', '10 feet (3 m)', 'about 550 lbs (247.5 kg)', '{"IQ":15,"ME":21,"MA":18,"PS":50,"PP":21,"PE":21,"PB":10,"Spd":44}', NULL, NULL, 325, 36, 62, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":3,"strike":8,"parry":13,"dodge":12,"roll":5,"pull":5,"disarm":4}', 'M.D.C. 325 is his own; separately, he can draw 597 M.D.C. from his Absurr Life Node into himself at any time. The two figures are stored apart and never summed. Eight physical attacks per melee plus two magic attacks through his Temporal Link, at most 10 spells a day. Also +3 to strike with a body block/tackle, +2 to save vs psionics, +8 to save vs Horror Factor, +3 to save vs poison and magic, +2 to save vs temporal magic, +30% to save vs coma/death, and a critical strike on 18-20. Strength and endurance are supernatural. Combat skills: martial arts, boxing and paired weapons. No attack damage is printed; none is derived.', NULL, 'The skills common to all Kydian Overlords and Powerlords, plus all military and many espionage skills at 98%.', 'Those of every Kydian, plus Bio-Wizard augmentation: enhanced attributes (already counted); Eyes of Eylor replacing his natural ones; two extra arms, each of the four with a retractable forearm blade; three symbiotic organisms, namely Absurr Life Node (Symbiote), Mindlink (Symbiote) and Temporal Link (Parasite), the last at power level four, which lets him see ripples in time left by temporal and most dimension-altering magic.', 'None beyond what his Temporal Link (Parasite) provides. P.P.E. 36.', 'Mind Block Auto-Defense, and limited telepathy reaching the elite Minions of Splugorth only. I.S.P. 62.', NULL, NULL, 'A Staff of Power and several D-Squad special weapons; he can draw on almost any Splugorth weapon, and may use greatest rune weapons when it is truly needed. Wears standard Overlord power armor altered for his extra arms and symbiotes, and carries Bio-Wizard and Techno-Wizard restraints for captives.', NULL, 'Blunt and curt, indifferent to anyone''s feelings, and openly objects to any High Lord order he thinks wrong, which costs him friends among them though not T''Lan. Sharp and tactical, he sizes up a threat quickly and answers it hard. Feared by Splynncryth''s enemies and by his own troops alike.', 'High Lord T''Lan, his superior; Powerlord Reytan, his second in command; Lord Splynncryth.', 'Dimensional Raiders, Shifters, True Atlanteans and temporal wizards.', 'A huge four-armed Kydian, heavily muscled. Born K''Ronn Sol on the harshest world of Splynncryth''s empire, he was neither the strongest nor the fastest of his peers but out-trained them all, and his tactical mind earned him an experimental augmentation offered only to an elite few. His Temporal Link gives him an edge over teleporters and time-benders but will kill him, probably within three to five years, and he accepted that knowingly. He commands the D-Squad Division, elite Minion units of 6 to 12 troops trained to hunt Dimensional Raiders, and can call on two full battalions besides. Powerlord Reytan, a 10th level Powerlord who has just received his own Temporal Link, is his second and is meant to succeed him; the book prints no stat block for Reytan. The heading spells the name Cronus; running text elsewhere in the book also spells it Cronos.', 'Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market p.55-56'),
('ren-the-hunter', 'Ren the Hunter', 'Alaren Aehizara of the Aerihman clan', 'Head of the D-Squad Pursuit Unit, Splynn', 'rifts', 'True Atlantean (Sunaj Assassin)', '10th level Sunaj Assassin (as printed)', 10, 'Diabolic', '78 years', '7 feet (2.1 m)', '220 lbs (99 kg)', '{"IQ":22,"ME":28,"MA":20,"PS":32,"PP":18,"PE":22,"PB":20,"Spd":33}', NULL, NULL, 157, 88, 105, NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"parry":7,"dodge":7,"pull":5,"roll":3,"disarm":3,"damage":21}', 'Six physical, tattoo magic or psionic attacks per melee round. Hand to Hand: Assassin and Boxing. Also a critical strike on 18-20, Death Blow, +6 to save vs magic, +4 to save vs Horror Factor, +7 to save vs psionics and +4 to save vs mind control. No attack damage is printed; none is derived.', NULL, 'All espionage and rogue skills, plus basic math, disguise, Lore: Demons and Monsters, Lore: Magic, and literacy in Greek, American and Dragonese, at 98%.', 'Those of every Sunaj Assassin: extended life span, faster P.P.E. recovery, immunity to physical transformation, senses vampires, operates dimensional pyramids, can sense Rifts, nexus points and ley lines, and can phase along a ley line.', 'The book counts 13 magic tattoos and names the Marks of Heritage plus eleven: Tattoo: Skull Coiled with Thorns (death touch), Tattoo: Flaming Shield, Tattoo: Heart Encircled by Chains (invulnerability), Tattoo: Chain with a Broken Link (strength), Tattoo: Eye of Mystic Knowledge (magic), Tattoo: Chain Encircling a Skull or Brain (psionic save), Tattoo: Beautiful Dancer (hypnotic gaze), Tattoo: Black Sun (darkness powers), Tattoo: Wolf''s Head with Glowing Eyes (hunting prowess), Tattoo: Skull Engulfed in Flames (fire powers), and Eye Impaled by a Dagger (blind; printed name, no catalog row). Each is the held catalog spelling of the printed name. P.P.E. 88.', 'Major psychic: Sixth Sense, See Aura, See the Invisible, Mind Block, Alter Aura and Impervious to Poison. Needs 12 or higher to save vs psionics. I.S.P. 105.', NULL, NULL, 'An Eylor Exploration Staff and several Bio-Wizard restraints at all times, with access to Splugorth weapons through his post and others through his contacts. Wears standard Sunaj body armor of 110 M.D.C. (printed for him; carried here, no gear row), and keeps a set of Overlord Bio-Wizard power armor for special occasions.', 'Well over a hundred million credits in gold and gems in a private hoard.', 'Treacherous even for a Sunaj: he helps destroy his own True Atlantean people and would sell out his clan, loyal only to himself. In the field he is patient and exact, never letting quarry know it is followed, and he handles his masters just as smoothly. Neither T''Lan nor Sunaj Lord Aerihza suspects his third employer, though each suspects him of serving the other.', 'High Lord T''Lan and Powerlord Cronus (his superiors); Sunaj Lord Aerihza and the Sunaj elders; a band of transdimensional raiders and mercenaries.', 'True Atlanteans; the Dimensional Raiders he hunts.', 'Tall and good-looking, dark-haired with deep green eyes, he never shows his real face in public; he prefers to pass as an old man with a long scar down the left of his face. As head of the D-Squad Pursuit Unit he chases raiders who flee the Market or hide in Splynn. He plays three sides: he reports to the Sunaj elders, tells Splynncryth what those elders plan, and for a cut of the take tips off a raiding band on when to strike the Market, then fails to catch them. Respected by Kydians and rare among Sunaj for it, he has escape plans ready for the day his deals come to light.', 'Rifts World Book 21: Splynn Dimensional Market p.56-58');

-- Read the result back. This script asserts its OWN rows and nothing else.
SELECT 'all 3 notable NPCs are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 3 AS want
  FROM notable_npcs WHERE slug IN ('high-lord-tlan', 'powerlord-cronus', 'ren-the-hunter');
SELECT 'and the notables 0' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 0 AS want
  FROM stat_attacks WHERE owner_kind = 'notable_npc' AND owner_slug IN ('high-lord-tlan', 'powerlord-cronus', 'ren-the-hunter');

